      ":question/problem": "![](images/ce/ce7563b04e7004ff36d66570db1f7ebee57d2357f49fd30cd5c5bf9bca11b72c.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Z$ lies on the segment $GN$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OG}=h$ and $\\overrightarrow{ON}=d$. The lengths satisfy $GZ:ZN=4:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OZ}$ in terms of $h$ and $d$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OG}=h\\qquad \\overrightarrow{ON}=d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $G$ through $O$ to $N$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\overrightarrow{GO}+\\overrightarrow{ON}=-h+d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $GZ:ZN=4:5$ gives $9$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GZ}=\\frac{4}{9}\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\frac{4}{9}(-h+d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to G\\to Z$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OZ}&=\\overrightarrow{OG}+\\overrightarrow{GZ}\\\\&=h+\\frac{4}{9}(-h+d)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{9}h+\\frac{4}{9}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
