      ":question/problem": "![](images/2a/2aff0727b19f7a32a04f35e316489b8f9b18675cf88841cfd59b52e845d6dd2b.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Z$ lies on the segment $XR$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OX}=f$ and $\\overrightarrow{OR}=u$. The lengths satisfy $XZ:ZR=3:4$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OZ}$ in terms of $f$ and $u$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OZ}=$ {{field-1}} $f+$ {{field-2}} $u$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX}=f\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OR}=u .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $X$ through $O$ to $R$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{XR}=\\overrightarrow{XO}+\\overrightarrow{OR}=-f+u.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $XZ:ZR=3:4$ gives $7$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{XZ}=\\frac{3}{7}\\overrightarrow{XR}=\\frac{3}{7}(-f+u).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to X\\to Z$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OZ}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XZ}\\\\&=f+\\frac{3}{7}(-f+u)\\\\&=\\frac{4}{7}f+\\frac{3}{7}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
